},{"bioguideId":"G000546","fullName":"Rep. Graves, Sam [R-MO-6]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-10-01","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"MO"},{"bioguideId":"L000397","fullName":"Rep. Lofgren, Zoe [D-CA-18]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-10-01","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CA"},{"bioguideId":"C001061","fullName":"Rep. Cleaver, Emanuel [D-MO-5]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-10-01","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"MO"},{"bioguideId":"G000604","fullName":"Rep. Goodlander, Maggie [D-NH-2]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-10-06","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NH"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-10-07T17:09:33+00:00","id":"hr5536-119","introducedDate":"2025-09-19","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-09-19","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Energy and Commerce."},"laws":[],"number":"5536","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Health","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"T000482","district":3,"fullName":"Rep. Trahan, Lori [D-MA-3]","party":"D","state":"MA"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-09-19","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><strong>Headache Education, Access, Diagnosis, and Care Health Equity Act or the HEADACHE Act</strong></p><p>This bill temporarily establishes a federal initiative, an advisory council, and related reporting to address headache disorders. The bill defines <em>headache disorder</em> as a medical condition for which a headache is a principal symptom, including primary conditions (e.g., tension-type headaches, migraines) and secondary conditions (i.e., headaches that are symptoms of other health conditions). &nbsp;</p><p>Specifically, the Department of Health and Human Services (HHS) must establish a coordinated federal initiative to take actions that advance research and improve care for headache disorders.&nbsp;</p><p>Also,&nbsp;HHS must establish an advisory council comprised of certain federal and non-federal members to advise HHS on headache disorders and hold annual research meetings.&nbsp;</p><p>Finally,&nbsp;HHS must annually report to Congress on headache disorders, including (1) an annually updated national plan, (2) evaluations of all relevant federally funded efforts, and (3) recommendations for priority actions.</p><p>The requirements of the bill sunset five years after the bill’s enactment.</p>","updateDate":"2026-10-05T16:22:14Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"HEADACHE Act","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-10-07T08:06:03Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-10-07T08:06:03Z"}
